d-suggestion","owner":"saransh2405","html_url":"https://github.com/saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":229842,"global_rank":112940,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19580},{"name":"codefellows/pph-helping-yourself","owner":"codefellows","html_url":"https://github.com/codefellows/pph-helping-yourself","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Partner Power Hour: Helping Yourself - Effectively Getting Assistance","topics":[],"score":229838,"global_rank":112945,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19581},{"name":"lsterzinger/atm115","owner":"lsterzinger","html_url":"https://github.com/lsterzinger/atm115","stars":0,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":229836,"global_rank":112951,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19582},{"name":"Wind010/pykudos","owner":"Wind010","html_url":"https://github.com/Wind010/pykudos","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":4,"language":"Python","description":"A python implementation of a praise tool","topics":[],"score":229832,"global_rank":112953,"on_pypi":false,"top_pypi":false,"python_rank":19583},{"name":"dmartin4506/leetcode-may-2024","owner":"dmartin4506","html_url":"https://github.com/dmartin4506/leetcod